  "note": "Triennial election of the 17 electoral divisions of Kilkeel rural district, one member each, polled on 5 June 1952. Four divisions were contested (Bryansford, Dunnaman, Glasdrummond, Maghera); the other thirteen members were returned unopposed. Russell, J.P., the outgoing member, held the seat by one vote after a recount."
